## 3️⃣ Class Diagram (UML – Core Entities)

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class Student {
        +string id
        +string name
        +string email
        +string rollNumber
    }

    class Course {
        +string id
        +string courseName
        +string code
    }

    class Marks {
        +string id
        +int score
    }

    class Attendance {
        +string id
        +date date
        +boolean present
    }

    Student "1" --> "many" Marks
    Student "1" --> "many" Attendance
    Course "1" --> "many" Marks
    Course "1" --> "many" Attendance
```

---

## 4️⃣ ER Diagram (Database Model)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    STUDENTS {
        string _id PK
        string name
        string email
        string roll_number
    }

    COURSES {
        string _id PK
        string course_name
        string course_code
    }

    MARKS {
        string _id PK
        string student_id FK
        string course_id FK
        int score
    }

    ATTENDANCE {
        string _id PK
        string student_id FK
        string course_id FK
        date date
        boolean present
    }

    STUDENTS ||--o{ MARKS : receives
    COURSES ||--o{ MARKS : has

    STUDENTS ||--o{ ATTENDANCE : attends
    COURSES ||--o{ ATTENDANCE : records
```

